{
 "schema": "beamio.firstContactChainTrust.v2",
 "decision": "first-contact trust of a chain-published key. v2: the record id is the ENCRYPTION SUBKEY's key id",
 "whitelist": [
  {
   "chainId": 224422,
   "contract": "0x684b0ac760cEE9c9b85de36d69746420648Cf9e2"
  }
 ],
 "rule": "With no pinned value: send directly (and record the PRIMARY key's fingerprint as the first pinned value) only when ALL hold: (1) the record's source is a whitelisted AddressPGP contract on its chain, (2) the address the read was made for equals the contact's address, (3) the AddressPGP record's userPgpKeyID is the key id (16 hex: low 64 bits of a v4 fingerprint, high 64 bits of a v6 one; or the full fingerprint) of the key that actually encrypts (the encryption subkey OpenPGP selects, the primary key when there is none). Otherwise first_fetch_pending. With a pinned value (primary fingerprint): equal -> send; different -> fingerprint_changed. A failed read is route_unconfirmed and is never trusted.",
 "fields": "read.fingerprint = primary key fingerprint; read.encryptionFingerprint = fingerprint of the encrypting (sub)key; read.userPgpKeyID = the chain record's field",
 "realData": "FC-01..03 are public keys of three accounts measured on the CoNET chain: the chain field equals the subkey's key id and differs from the primary's",
 "nativeNote": "The native SDKs hold no contact trust rule: they encrypt to the key the page hands them and take the receipt route table the page builds. The page's decision (this vector set) is the single rule; a native implementation that ever decides first-contact trust must pass these vectors.",
